<title>USA: Great American cleared to buy back shares.</title>
<headline>Great American cleared to buy back shares.</headline>
<dateline>CHAMPAIGN, Ill. 1996-12-10</dateline>
<text>
<p>Great American Bancorp Inc said Tuesday it received regulatory clearance to buy back up to five percent, or 92,630 shares, of its outstanding common stock.</p>
<p>The board of the company previously authorized, subject to regulatory clearance, the repurchase of up to five percent of the company's 1,852,606 outstanding shares.</p>
<p>Great American, parent of First Federal Savings Bank of Champaign-Urbana, said the repurchases will begin soon after the release of the company's earnings for the quarter and year ended December 31, 1996.</p>
<p>		  ((-- Chicago newsdesk 312 408-8787))</p>
